{# =====================================================
   FAQ — same aboutFaq.json data, restyled to the sitewide
   accordion recipe used on contact.njk/homepage-v2.njk.
   Bottom padding trimmed (pb, not py) since the next section
   (Infrastructure-Level AI) brings its own top padding — the
   two stacking at full py-20+py-20 left an oversized gap at
   just this one boundary, without affecting the section's own
   top spacing or any other section-to-section transition.
   ===================================================== #}
<section class="px-4 pt-12 pb-6 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-8 lg:px-8 lg:pt-20 lg:pb-10" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-content">
    <div class="mb-10 max-w-2xl md:mb-12 mx-auto text-center" data-reveal>
      <span class="mb-4 block font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-[#9CA3AF]">
        Support
      </span>
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] sm:text-[32px] lg:text-[36px]">
        Häufig gestellte Fragen
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl" data-reveal x-data="{ activeIndex: null }">
      <div class="divide-y divide-navy-100" data-reveal-stagger>
        {% for item in aboutFaq %}
          <div class="py-5">
            <button
              @click="activeIndex = (activeIndex === {{ loop.index }}) ? null : {{ loop.index }}"
              class="flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-4 text-left group"
              :aria-expanded="activeIndex === {{ loop.index }} ? 'true' : 'false'"
              aria-controls="about-faq-answer-{{ loop.index }}"
            >
              <span class="text-[16px] font-medium leading-snug text-[#111827] transition-colors group-hover:text-navy-600 sm:text-[17px]">
                {{ item.question }}
              </span>
              <span class="flex h-6 w-6 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-navy-200 text-navy-500 transition-transform duration-200" :class="activeIndex === {{ loop.index }} ? 'rotate-45' : ''">
                <svg class="h-3 w-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4"></path>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div
              id="about-faq-answer-{{ loop.index }}"
              x-show="activeIndex === {{ loop.index }}"
              x-transition:enter="transition ease-out duration-200"
              x-transition:enter-start="opacity-0 -translate-y-2"
              x-transition:enter-end="opacity-100 translate-y-0"
              x-transition:leave="transition ease-in duration-150"
              x-transition:leave-start="opacity-100 translate-y-0"
              x-transition:leave-end="opacity-0 -translate-y-2"
              class="overflow-hidden"
            >
              <p class="pt-3 pr-10 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] sm:text-[15px]">{{ item.answer }}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# =====================================================
   INFRASTRUCTURE-LEVEL AI COMPARISON
   Recovered from commit 8d68e55 (SEOAI expanded-content
   block, since removed) and re-homed into the v2 layout.
   Aligned to the FAQ section's own mx-auto max-w-3xl reading
   column directly above it — it previously sat in the wider
   max-w-content container with no inner centering, so its left
   edge started well before the FAQ column's left edge.
   ===================================================== #}
<section class="px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-20" aria-labelledby="ai-infra-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="ai-infra-heading" class="text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] sm:text-[32px] lg:text-[36px]">KI auf Infrastrukturebene, keine Wrapper</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] sm:text-[17px]">
      <p>Die meisten KI-Anbieter bauen eine dünne Schicht über eine bestehende Modell-API — einen "Wrapper", der eine Chat-Oberfläche hinzufügt, aber kaum mehr. Zunkiree Labs geht einen anderen Weg: Wir entwerfen und besitzen die zugrunde liegende KI-Infrastruktur selbst, von RAG-Pipelines und Wissenssystemen bis zu den Datengrundlagen, die sie antreiben, sodass das System mit der Nutzung weiter an Wert gewinnt, statt eine einmalige Integration zu bleiben.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 mb-2 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-gray-200">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-gray-50">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-gray-900">Merkmal</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-gray-900">Alternative</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-gray-900">Diese Option</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200">
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900">Grundlage</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">API-Wrapper über einem Drittanbieter-Modell</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Eigene KI-native Infrastruktur (RAG-Pipelines, Wissenssysteme)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900">Datenreife</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Ad hoc, Projekt für Projekt</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Skalierbare Datenpipelines und KI-fähige Infrastruktur von Anfang an integriert</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900">Zusammenarbeitsmodell</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Einmalige Projektlieferung</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Fortlaufende Plattform, deren Wert mit der Zeit wächst</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900">Leistungsumfang</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600">Einzelne Punktlösung</td>
